* SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
* IHP SG13G2, pre-layout DDR1 SSTL-2 DQ pad, 1.2 V core / 2.5 V I/O.
* Active-high OE is core-domain. PU_OK is a 2.5 V supervisor input: hold
* low until both supplies are valid, and drop it before either rail falls.
* PAD must remain within the I/O rails; this is not an unpowered fail-safe pad.
* VREF is the distributed board reference, after its separate entry pad.
* IO MOS w is total width, ng divides that width into fingers.

.subckt ihp_sstl2_io_inv A Y VP VN params: wn=2.4u wp=4.8u fingers=2
XN Y A VN VN sg13_hv_nmos w={wn} l=0.45u ng={fingers}
XP Y A VP VP sg13_hv_pmos w={wp} l=0.40u ng={fingers}
.ends ihp_sstl2_io_inv

.subckt ihp_sstl2_io_nand A B Y VP VN wn=4.8u wp=4.8u
XNA Y A N VN sg13_hv_nmos w={wn} l=0.45u ng=2
XNB N B VN VN sg13_hv_nmos w={wn} l=0.45u ng=2
XPA Y A VP VP sg13_hv_pmos w={wp} l=0.40u ng=2
XPB Y B VP VP sg13_hv_pmos w={wp} l=0.40u ng=2
.ends ihp_sstl2_io_nand

.subckt ihp_sstl2_core_inv A Y VDD VSS wn=3u wp=6u
XN Y A VSS VSS sg13_lv_nmos w={wn} l=0.13u ng=2
XP Y A VDD VDD sg13_lv_pmos w={wp} l=0.13u ng=3
.ends ihp_sstl2_core_inv

* Only the HV pull-down gates see the core voltage. The core complement
* driver is entirely inside the low-voltage domain; its drain never sees IO.
* Size the ratioed latch for the slow 1.08 V core drive, not nominal only.
.subckt ihp_sstl2_up A Y YB VDD VSS VDDIO VSSIO
XCINV A AB VDD VSS ihp_sstl2_core_inv wn=5u wp=15u
XNA YB A  VSSIO VSSIO sg13_hv_nmos w=40u l=0.45u ng=10
XNB Y  AB VSSIO VSSIO sg13_hv_nmos w=40u l=0.45u ng=10
XPA Y  YB VDDIO VDDIO sg13_hv_pmos w=5u l=0.50u ng=2
XPB YB Y  VDDIO VDDIO sg13_hv_pmos w=5u l=0.50u ng=2
.ends ihp_sstl2_up

.subckt ihp130_sstl2_dq OUT OE IN PAD VREF PU_OK VDD VSS VDDIO VSSIO
* RX: resistively fed current mirror, NMOS input pair, PMOS mirror load.
* PAD > VREF raises SENSE. The NAND inverts and qualifies the decision.
XRBIAS VDDIO BIAS VSSIO rhigh w=1.2u l=13u
XBIAS BIAS BIAS VSSIO VSSIO sg13_hv_nmos w=3u l=0.65u ng=2
XTAIL TAIL BIAS VSSIO VSSIO sg13_hv_nmos w=3u l=0.65u ng=2
XRP MIRROR PAD  TAIL VSSIO sg13_hv_nmos w=5u l=0.55u ng=2
XRR SENSE  VREF TAIL VSSIO sg13_hv_nmos w=5u l=0.55u ng=2
XLP MIRROR MIRROR VDDIO VDDIO sg13_hv_pmos w=4u l=0.55u ng=2
XLR SENSE  MIRROR VDDIO VDDIO sg13_hv_pmos w=4u l=0.55u ng=2
XDET SENSE PU_OK DEC_B VDDIO VSSIO ihp_sstl2_io_nand
* Resistively loaded HV pull-down translates DEC_B without a 2.5 V gate
* on any oxide in the core inverter. The only core-facing RX_LEVEL node
* is pulled up to the 1.2 V rail. This draws core current for a low read.
XRDOWN VDD RX_LEVEL VSS rhigh w=1.2u l=10u
XDOWN RX_LEVEL DEC_B VSS VSS sg13_hv_nmos w=5u l=0.45u ng=2
XRXB0 RX_LEVEL RX_B VDD VSS ihp_sstl2_core_inv
XRXB1 RX_B IN VDD VSS ihp_sstl2_core_inv

* TX: independently move data and core OE into the I/O domain. Qualify
* OE after the shifter so PU_OK=0 dominates even if its latch is undefined.
XDATA OUT DATA_H DATA_L VDD VSS VDDIO VSSIO ihp_sstl2_up
XOE   OE  OE_H   OE_L   VDD VSS VDDIO VSSIO ihp_sstl2_up
XGUARD OE_H PU_OK EN_B VDDIO VSSIO ihp_sstl2_io_nand wn=8u wp=9.6u
XEN EN_B EN VDDIO VSSIO ihp_sstl2_io_inv
XUP DATA_H EN P_B VDDIO VSSIO ihp_sstl2_io_nand wn=10u wp=8u
XDN DATA_L EN N_B VDDIO VSSIO ihp_sstl2_io_nand wn=8u wp=9.6u
XPPRE P_B P1 VDDIO VSSIO ihp_sstl2_io_inv wn=11u wp=25u fingers=4
XPG P1 PG VDDIO VSSIO ihp_sstl2_io_inv wn=44u wp=40u fingers=8
XNG N_B NG VDDIO VSSIO ihp_sstl2_io_inv wn=24u wp=58u fingers=6
XDRVH DRIVER PG VDDIO VDDIO sg13_hv_pmos w=200u l=0.40u ng=40
XDRVL DRIVER NG VSSIO VSSIO sg13_hv_nmos w=72u l=0.45u ng=18
XRDRIVER DRIVER PAD VSSIO rppd w=8u l=0.6u

* PDK pad diodes for nominal loading/leakage, not qualified HBM/CDM or a
* rail clamp. A separately validated rail clamp is a pad-ring obligation.
XESDHI VDDIO PAD VSSIO diodevdd_2kv
XESDLO VDDIO PAD VSSIO diodevss_2kv
.ends ihp130_sstl2_dq
